{
  "raw_html": "<button type='button' role='link' class='btn btn-link p-0 text-start' id='link_1' aria-label=\" Parvinder Singh versus Directorate of Enforcement pdf\"  class='noToken' href='#' onclick=javascript:open_pdf('1','2026','2026_6_486_508','2026INSC519'); ><font size='4'> <strong>PARVINDER SINGH<span class='fst-italic'> versus </span>DIRECTORATE OF ENFORCEMENT </strong>- <span class='escrText'>[2026] 6 S.C.R. 486</span><span class='ncDisplay'>2026 INSC 519</span><input type='hidden' id='cnr' value=ESCR010001782026></button></font><br> Issue for Consideration The present appeal has been preferred against the judgment dated 19.05.2025 passed by the High Court wherein, an issue with respect to the scope and applicability of the first proviso to s.223(1) of the Bharatiya Nagarik Suraksha Sanhita, 2023 (BNSS) had arisen, while where the prosecution complaint under the Prevention of Money Laundering Act, 2002 (PMLA) had been filed prior to the date of commencement of the BNSS. Headnotes&dagger; Bharatiya Nagarik Suraksha Sanhita, 2023 &ndash; ss.2(1)(k), 4, 5, 210, First proviso to s.223(1), 531 &ndash; Prevention of<br><strong class='caseDetailsTD' ><span style='color:#212F3D' > Decision Date :</span><font color='green'> 19-05-2026</font><span style='color:#212F3D' > | Case No :</span><font color='green'> CRIMINAL APPEAL No. 2678/2026</font><span style='color:#212F3D' > | Disposal Nature :</span><font color='green'> Appeal(s) allowed</font>   <span style='color:#212F3D' > |  Bench :</span><font color='green'> 1 Judge</font></strong><div class='row my-1 mt-2 border bg-light'><div class='col-auto'><a href='#' class='btn btn-outline-secondary btn-sm my-1' onclick=open_splitview('1','2026','2026_6_486_508','2026INSC519','S')><i <i class='fas fa-columns me-2'></i>Split view</a></div><div class='col-auto'><a href='#' class='btn btn-outline-secondary btn-sm my-1' onclick=open_splitview('1','2026','2026_6_486_508','2026INSC519','H'); ><i class='fas fa-file-alt me-2'></i